  :adr/id "2607252600"
  :adr/title "ABI is the implementation-free Kotoba execution contract"
  :adr/status :accepted
  :adr/date "2026-07-25"
  :adr/body "Kotoba Components need one portable definition of worlds, explicit capabilities, artifact identity, and admission shape. Duplicating these in compiler, runtime, authority, and fleet control allows semantic drift; making one implementation depend on another would invert authority. Create kotoba-lang/abi as the versioned source of WIT, schemas, canonical encodings, and conformance vectors. It contains no executable policy or host implementation. The compiler consumes it to emit Components and manifests. Kototama consumes it to validate, compile, link, and execute. Aiueos consumes it to decide grants and construct named providers. Murakumo consumes it only to validate deployment declarations and observe identities; it cannot manufacture grants or provider bindings. Dependencies point from each implementation to abi, never among implementations for contract sharing. Shared executable code is extracted only after it has independent consumers and must remain below the authority boundary."}]
